These headers are VERBATIM copies from the Falcon Player source tree.  They
are here so the plugin's override set can be compiled against the REAL base
classes on both plugin-API shapes without an FPP checkout.  Nothing in this
directory is hand-written except stub/, which stands in for third-party
libraries FPP itself pulls in (jsoncpp, libhttpserver, drogon).

  v80/Plugin.h       <- git show 8.0:src/Plugin.h
  v8/Plugin.h        <- git show 8.5.1:src/Plugin.h
  vmaster/Plugin.h   <- git show master:src/Plugin.h
  vmaster/fpphttp.h  <- git show master:src/fpphttp.h

  8.0     bd91a86c410dce6f24b71bd73201d3b57012367d
  8.5.1   0f9c98a9ecb939ea4c69050b45174fa248ac8c33
  master  b58bfef51460b2b5be2bbe1b5a98bb700b8fe9cb

Refresh with:  make -C test refresh-fppapi FPP_SRC=/path/to/fpp

Why both shapes matter: releases up to and including 10.x declare
`registerApis(httpserver::webserver*)` against real libhttpserver; master's
drogon migration keeps that signature as a [[deprecated]] shim that routes into
drogon, and adds a no-argument form.  The two libraries also differ in the
top-level cv-qualification of render_GET's return type — a mismatch there is a
hard error, not a warning, so the plugin derives the type from the base with
decltype instead of asserting it.  stub/httpserver.hpp is compiled BOTH ways
(PM_STUB_CONST_RETURN) to prove that derivation binds under either.

`playlistInserted` — the callback the whole §13.1 mirror rests on — was added
to FPP on 2024-12-07 and first shipped in 8.5.  It is absent from 8.0 and 7.0,
which pluginInfo.json still declares support for; v8/Plugin.h is pinned at
8.5.1 because that is the OLDEST released line carrying it, and it is one of
the two rig boxes.
